    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 2.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.c"/><pb n="492–495" ed="#liebermann"/>E si aucuns vescunte<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.d"/> u provost mesfait as humes<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.e"/> . . ., ende e de ceo seit ateint devant justise le . . .<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="f" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.f"/>, forfeit est a duble de ceo que auter fust forfeit.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="492–495" ed="#liebermann"/>Et se alquens, u quens<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.c-2"/> u provost<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="32" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.32"/>, mesfeist<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="33" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.33"/> as homes de sa baillie, e de ço fuist<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="34" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.34"/> atint de la justice lu roi, forfait fust<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="35" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.35"/> a<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="36" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.36"/> duble de ce que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="37" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.37"/> altre fust forfait.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="492–495" ed="#liebermann"/>[2, 1] Quodsi uicecomes uel prepositi<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.a"/> conuicti fuerint coram iustitiar. regis erga homines sue ballie deliquisse, duplo forisfactum maius reportabit, quam alii in pari delicto.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="2.1" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="252" ed="#robertson"/>E si aucuns vescunte u provost mesfait as humes [de sa baillie], e de ceo seit ateint devant justise le [rei], forfeit est a duble de ceo que auter fust forfeit.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="492–495" ed="#liebermann"/>2, 1. Und wenn ein Sheriff (jemand, entweder Graf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="k" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.de1.k"/> <hi rend="italic">I</hi>) oder Amtmann den Leuten seines Amtsbezirks Missethat zufügt und dessen vor (von <hi rend="italic">I</hi>) dem Königsrichter überführt wird, ist er<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="l" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.de1.l"/> in Busse verfallen<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="m" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.de1.m"/> zum doppelten<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_2-1.lnote.de.1"/> dessen, was ein anderer verwirkt hätte.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">2, 1. And if a sheriff (someone, either count <hi rend="italic">I</hi>) or reeve does wrong to the people of his district and is convicted of it before (by <hi rend="italic">I</hi>) the king's justice, he has incurred a compensation of double what another would have forfeited.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="253" ed="#robertson"/>And if any sheriff or mayor does injury to the men in his jurisdiction and is convicted of this in the King's Court, he shall pay double the fine payable by any other person.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 252–253 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 492–495, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">2,2 <hi rend="italic">setzt vor</hi> 2,1 <hi rend="italic">L, vielleicht originaler, da zu II Cn.</hi> 14 <hi rend="italic">f. näher</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">L places 2,2 before 2,1, perhaps more originally, since closer to II Cn. 14 f.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">vesquens [<hi rend="italic">vgl. Suchier</hi> Altfranz. Gram. § 46] <hi rend="italic">hatte wohl F</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">F probably had vesquens [cf. Suchier Altfranz. Gram. § 46]</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">de sa baillie <hi rend="italic">ergänzen Edd. aus IL;</hi> ende <hi rend="italic">zu streichen</hi> (<hi rend="italic">als Dittographie des folgenden</hi> e de?)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">de sa baillie supplied by edd. from IL; ende to be deleted (as a dittography of the following e de?)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.f" n="f" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> rei <hi rend="italic">aus IL; vgl.</hi> 17, 3; <hi rend="italic">Hk verband wohl</hi> le forfeit <hi rend="italic">als Substantiv</hi> (<hi rend="italic">so MATZKE</hi> Lois de Guill. <hi rend="italic">S.</hi> 3), <hi rend="italic">hinter</hi> justise ‘des Königs’ <hi rend="italic">hinzudenkend, wie</hi> 31</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply rei from IL; cf. 17, 3; Hk probably construed le forfeit as a noun (so MATZKE Lois de Guill. p. 3), understanding ‘the king's’ after justise, as in 31</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.c-2" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">falsch</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wrong</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.32" n="32" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">statt</hi> u. p.: vxuost <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">instead of u. p.: vxuost Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.33" n="33" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">messeist <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">messeist Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.34" n="34" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">suist <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">suist Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.35" n="35" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sust <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sust Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.36" n="36" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">u. <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">u. Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.37" n="37" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">492</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">comme <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">comme Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.de1.k" n="k" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">493</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">diese Lesart ist falsch: sie lässt den unumgänglichen</hi> Sheriff <hi rend="italic">fort und giebt dem Grafen statt</hi> comté <hi rend="italic">nur eine</hi> baillie</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">this reading is wrong: it omits the indispensable sheriff and gives the earl only a baillie instead of a comté</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.de1.l" n="l" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">493</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Pronomen fehlt auch vor</hi> rendist 1, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Pronoun also lacking before rendist 1, 1</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.de1.m" n="m" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">493</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Particip vor Hilfszeitwort auch</hi> 18; <hi rend="italic">Particip</hi> forfeit <hi rend="italic">auch</hi> 47</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Participle before auxiliary verb also in 18; participle forfeit also in 47</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">495</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-tus conuictus fuerit <hi rend="italic">bessert THORPE</hi> Ancient laws</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-tus conuictus fuerit emended by THORPE Ancient laws</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_2-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">286</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dieses Doppelstrafgeld auch sonst; <hi rend="italic">s. Gl</hi> Amtsvergehen 3a. b; Vogt 11d. 24</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">This double fine occurs elsewhere too; see <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Amtsvergehen 3a. b; Vogt 11d. 24</seg></note>
      </div>
